  "stem": "The table shows the stopping distance \\(d(v)\\), in meters, of a car traveling at a speed of \\(v\\) meters per second when the brakes are applied. The stopping distance is given by \\(d(v) = kv^{2}\\), where \\(k\\) is a constant. What is the value of \\(d(40)\\)?",
  "figure": {
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Stopping distance",
    "columns": [
      "Speed, v (m/s)",
      "Stopping distance, d(v) (m)"
    ],
    "rows": [
      [
        "10",
        "5"
      ],
      [
        "20",
        "20"
      ],
      [
        "30",
        "45"
      ]
    ]
  },
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "80"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Find \\(k\\) from any row: \\(d(10) = k(10)^{2} = 100k = 5\\), so \\(k = \\frac{1}{20}\\).",
    "Check: \\(\\frac{1}{20}(20)^{2} = 20\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{20}(30)^{2} = 45\\), matching the table.",
    "\\(d(40) = \\frac{1}{20}(40)^{2} = \\frac{1{,}600}{20} = 80\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "v, k = symbols('v k')\nrows = [(int(r[0]), int(r[1])) for r in figure['rows']]\nks = {Rational(b, a**2) for a, b in rows}\nassert ks == {Rational(1, 20)}\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [Rational(1, 20)*40**2]",
